cast requires tensor or prim type, got `prec`
Blocker: chelis#2151. The checker rejects a scalar source typed by a
Float-bounded binder in `cast`/`cast_trunc`, while the tensor form with the
same binder is accepted. [05-OP-6] says the two surfaces have identical
semantics. The same rejection covers `cast(x, int64)` and `cast(x, f64)`.
On pass: in nautilus#69's Float-generic Nautilus.Stats, replace the
length-1-tensor truncation helper with a direct `cast_trunc(x, int64)`, and
archive the chelis#2151 entry in docs/UPSTREAM_BUGS.md in the same change
set. A pass here does NOT unblock nautilus#69 by itself: the downstream C
build blocker in docs/UPSTREAM_BUGS.md must also clear.
